#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.39.4 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:6
msgid ""
"This addresses the security issues CVE-2024-32002, CVE-2024-32004, "
"CVE-2024-32020 and CVE-2024-32021."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:9
msgid ""
"This release also backports fixes necessary to let the CI builds pass "
"successfully."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.39.3"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:14
msgid "CVE-2024-32002:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recursive clones on case-insensitive filesystems that support symbolic\n"
"links are susceptible to case confusion that can be exploited to\n"
"execute just-cloned code during the clone operation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:20
msgid "CVE-2024-32004:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Repositories can be configured to execute arbitrary code during local\n"
"clones. To address this, the ownership checks introduced in v2.30.3\n"
"are now extended to cover cloning local repositories.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:26
msgid "CVE-2024-32020:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:32
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Local clones may end up hardlinking files into the target repository's\n"
"object database when source and target repository reside on the same\n"
"disk. If the source repository is owned by a different user, then\n"
"those hardlinked files may be rewritten at any point in time by the\n"
"untrusted user.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:34
msgid "CVE-2024-32021:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When cloning a local source repository that contains symlinks via the\n"
"filesystem, Git may create hardlinks to arbitrary user-readable files\n"
"on the same filesystem as the target repository in the objects/\n"
"directory.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:41
msgid "CVE-2024-32465:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is supposed to be safe to clone untrusted repositories, even those\n"
"unpacked from zip archives or tarballs originating from untrusted\n"
"sources, but Git can be tricked to run arbitrary code as part of the\n"
"clone.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:49
msgid ""
"Defense-in-depth: submodule: require the submodule path to contain "
"directories only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:52
msgid ""
"Defense-in-depth: clone: when symbolic links collide with directories, keep "
"the latter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:54
msgid "Defense-in-depth: clone: prevent hooks from running during a clone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:56
msgid "Defense-in-depth: core.hooksPath: add some protection while cloning."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:58
msgid "Defense-in-depth: fsck: warn about symlink pointing inside a gitdir."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:60
msgid "Various fix-ups on HTTP tests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:62
msgid "Test update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:66
msgid ""
"HTTP Header redaction code has been adjusted for a newer version of cURL "
"library that shows its traces differently from earlier versions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:69
msgid ""
"Fix was added to work around a regression in libcURL 8.7.0 (which has "
"already been fixed in their tip of the tree)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:71
msgid "Replace macos-12 used at GitHub CI with macos-13."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:73
msgid "ci(linux-asan/linux-ubsan): let's save some time"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:77
msgid ""
"Tests with LSan from time to time seem to emit harmless message that makes "
"our tests unnecessarily flakey; we work it around by filtering the "
"uninteresting output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.39.4.txt:79
msgid ""
"Update GitHub Actions jobs to avoid warnings against using deprecated "
"version of Node.js."
msgstr ""
